        question: "What is the standard rule of thumb for calculating asphalt tonnage?",
        answer: "The universal industry rule of thumb is 110 lbs per square yard per inch of compacted thickness (approx 2.47 tons per 100 sq ft at 2 inches depth). This derives from a standard compacted bulk density of 145 to 148 lbs per cubic foot.",
